From: egui-aros
Subject: [PATCH] aros-gui-sys: pictures on the clipboard (datatypes read, ILBM write)

Repository: aros-development-team/AROS bf7075aab8480cf36bdc13b4382ccbd6098c8a0d,
  tools/crosstools/rust/crates/aros-gui-sys, with 0001-0003.
Date: 2026-11-07
Problem: the glue had only clipboard text. A program could not paste the
  picture another AROS program (AROS Capture, MultiView) put on the
  clipboard, and egui-winit, which reads pictures through its clipboard when
  Cmd/Ctrl+V finds no text (Event::PasteImage), had nothing to call on AROS.
Rationale: clipboard glue belongs in one place, below winit and egui-winit.
  Reading goes through datatypes (DTST_CLIPBOARD, picture group, PMODE_V43,
  PDTM_READPIXELARRAY in RGBA over whole rows, as picture.datatype's
  conversion loop requires), after a look at the FORM type with iffparse so
  that an empty or text clipboard is told apart from an unreadable picture.
  The caller allocates the pixels after a size check (16384 a side, 256 MiB).
  Writing is a 24-bit ILBM (BMHD and ByteRun1 BODY, planes R0-7, G0-7,
  B0-7) through iffparse; datatypes' DTM_COPY is not needed. Libraries are
  opened per call. Reading never changes the clipboard.
Scope: new functions (src/clippic.c, `clipboard::read_picture`,
  `write_picture`, `encode_ilbm`); links amiga.lib for DoMethodA.
Upstream-status: candidate for the AROS crate store (not submitted).
Verification: host tests (ILBM encoder decoded back pixel-exact at odd
  widths, ByteRun1, limits); C compiled with -Wall -Wextra
  -Werror=implicit-function-declaration for x86_64 ABIv11, x86_64 ABIv1 and
  aarch64; runtime (as egui-aros' clipboard_image before the move): AROS One
  1.3, Capture ILBM read pixel-exact, write/read at 17..2400 px, damaged,
  cut and oversized pictures reported.
Removal: when the AROS crate store carries an equivalent change.
